Optimiser V0.50 has the same command line as previous versions, but with
the added DAYS parameter.  The DAYS parameter specifies which messages to
delete.  ie. if DAYS=30 then EVERY message in EVERY section older then the
current date, minus 30 days will be deleted.

eg. Optimiser PATH1 PATH2 DAYS -V
    Optimiser BBS:Messages/ ram: 45 -V

Optimise the message base within "BBS:Messages/", outputing the results to
"ram:", with ALL messages older than 45 days old, being deleted.  All of
this shown in a VERY verbose manner :-)

*NOTE* "PATH1" and "PATH2" are STILL compulsory, with "DAYS" and "-V"
being optional parameters.  Typing "Optimiser" without any parameters, or
incorrect parameters, will show a usage template. 

The Optimisers "Fixing" abilities have now been completely verified!  That
is, it is able to fix corrupt MAXS messages bases!  It does this by
completely rebuilding every facet of the message base from scratch!  ie
None of the original section counts, active message counts, etc, are used
in the optimised message base.  They are all built from scratch, thus
enabling the Optimiser to fix every corrupt message base I've been able to
cause :-D  This function of the Optimiser was always there, just never
completely verified, (due to the lack of test subjects, ie corrupt message
bases), now it has been put through its paces and seems to work very well!  It
is pretty much guaranteed to make any corrupt message base, which causes a
GURU, Software Error/Task Held, or Message Base Corrupted Error to appear,
completely readable and usable by MAXS. 

*NOTE* It cannot and will not repair actual message text content, (this is
almost impossible, with the current MAXS message structure :-(), ie messages that
have garbled text, will not be ungarbled.  But they will become readable
and NOT cause MAXS to crash in anyway, once passed through the Optimiser!

Installer V0.50, this little prog actually allows the NEW message base to
be installed into a currently running MAXS. It simply has two options,
"PATH" and "-V"

eg. Installer PATH -V
    Installer BBS:Messages/message.index -V

The "PATH" parameter is the actual path/filename to the NEW message.index
file that you want MAXS to recognise.  The "-V" option is once again a
Verbose option, which in this case is a little more useful than the
Optimiser's Verbose option.  

To use it with the Optimiser a very simple script is needed.  A simple
example follows, chop 'n' change to suit your requirements!

eg.  Optimiser BBS:Messages/ temp: 60
     copy BBS:Messages/#? temp:
     copy temp:#?.opt BBS:Messages/
     rename BBS:Messages/message.text.opt BBS:Messages/message.text
     rename BBS:Messages/message.data.opt BBS:Messages/message.data
     rename BBS:Messages/message.index.opt BBS:Messages/message.index
     Installer BBS:Messages/message.index


OK, the reason for having the Installer as a seperate program, are
twofold!  Originally it was an automatic part of the Optimiser, but the
need arose to allow optional control over it for:

1: Fixing corrupted message bases, the last thing you want is a "hopefully
fixed" corrupted message base, being automatically installed into your
currently running copy of MAXS!

2:Much more flexible backups available of unoptimised and optimised
message bases!

